{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.a832d0ecdc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-617","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Delacroix is a Kenyan composer.</li><li>In 2003, Delacroix wrote <i>Open Harbor</i>, an opera.</li><li><i>Open Harbor</i> uses only percussion instruments in its second movement.</li><li><i>Open Harbor</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.</li><li>Delacroix trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Open Harbor.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Open Harbor</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.","<i>Open Harbor</i> was written in 2003.","<i>Open Harbor</i>, an opera by Delacroix, uses only percussion instruments in its second movement.","Ayumi Delacroix trained as a concert pianist."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.a27172f3fe","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-619","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Quintero is an Indian filmmaker.</li><li>In 2021, Quintero released <i>Wild Harbor</i>, an animated film.</li><li><i>Wild Harbor</i> features only nonprofessional actors.</li><li><i>Wild Harbor</i> became one of the most-watched films of its year.</li><li>Quintero studied anthropology before turning to film.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Wild Harbor was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Wild Harbor</i>, an animated film by Quintero, features only nonprofessional actors.","<i>Wild Harbor</i> became one of the most-watched films of its year.","Dmitri Quintero is an Indian filmmaker.","<i>Wild Harbor</i> was released in 2021."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.6e1add2371","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-631","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Brennan is a Ghanaian chef.</li><li>In 2023, Brennan published <i>Open Hours</i>, a cookbook.</li><li><i>Open Hours</i> organizes its recipes by season.</li><li><i>Open Hours</i> inspired a popular cooking show.</li><li>Brennan learned to cook in a grandparent's kitchen.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Open Hours.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Open Hours</i> inspired a popular cooking show.","Nadia Brennan learned to cook in a grandparent's kitchen.","<i>Open Hours</i> was published in 2023.","<i>Open Hours</i>, a cookbook by Brennan, organizes its recipes by season."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.38807ed9ee","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-635","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Sato is an Irish composer.</li><li>In 1977, Sato wrote <i>Salt Season</i>, a symphony.</li><li><i>Salt Season</i> incorporates recordings of ocean waves.</li><li><i>Salt Season</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.</li><li>Sato trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Salt Season was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Salt Season</i>, a symphony by Sato, incorporates recordings of ocean waves.","<i>Salt Season</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.","<i>Salt Season</i> was written in 1977.","Chen Sato is an Irish composer."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.7c4c77df78","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-635","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Sato is an Irish composer.</li><li>In 1977, Sato wrote <i>Salt Season</i>, a symphony.</li><li><i>Salt Season</i> incorporates recordings of ocean waves.</li><li><i>Salt Season</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.</li><li>Sato trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of Salt Season.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Salt Season</i> was written in 1977.","Chen Sato trained as a concert pianist.","<i>Salt Season</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.","<i>Salt Season</i>, a symphony by Sato, incorporates recordings of ocean waves."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.c2565719fd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-637","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Rahman is a Vietnamese architect.</li><li>In 1974, Rahman designed the Fairhaven Community Center.</li><li>The Fairhaven Community Center is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.</li><li>The Fairhaven Community Center won a national design award.</li><li>Rahman trained at a design school in Copenhagen.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when the Fairhaven Community Center was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Fairhaven Community Center, designed by Rahman, is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.","Amara Rahman is a Vietnamese architect.","The Fairhaven Community Center won a national design award.","The Fairhaven Community Center was designed in 1974."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.0f85a6a8d1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-640","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mateo Iyer is a Filipino engineer.</li><li>In 1971, Iyer developed the ClearFlow Water Filter.</li><li>The ClearFlow Water Filter costs less than ten dollars to produce.</li><li>The ClearFlow Water Filter won an international innovation prize.</li><li>Iyer worked for years at a rural health clinic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of the ClearFlow Water Filter.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The ClearFlow Water Filter was developed in 1971.","The ClearFlow Water Filter won an international innovation prize.","Mateo Iyer worked for years at a rural health clinic.","The ClearFlow Water Filter, developed by Iyer, costs less than ten dollars to produce."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.f702d3f74f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-641","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Iyer is a Filipino choreographer.</li><li>In 2005, Iyer created <i>Wild Field</i>, a dance piece.</li><li><i>Wild Field</i> is performed without any music.</li><li><i>Wild Field</i> won a major dance award.</li><li>Iyer trained in both ballet and traditional dance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Wild Field.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Wild Field</i> was created in 2005.","<i>Wild Field</i> won a major dance award.","Samuel Iyer trained in both ballet and traditional dance.","<i>Wild Field</i>, a dance piece by Iyer, is performed without any music."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.6dada6f425","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-p-649","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Rahman is a Nigerian composer.</li><li>In 1993, Rahman wrote <i>Paper House</i>, a symphony.</li><li><i>Paper House</i> uses only percussion instruments in its second movement.</li><li><i>Paper House</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.</li><li>Rahman trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Paper House.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Paper House</i>, a symphony by Rahman, uses only percussion instruments in its second movement.","<i>Paper House</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.","<i>Paper House</i> was written in 1993.","Viktor Rahman trained as a concert pianist."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.cdaa9e54e5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-57","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Kowalski is a zoologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","To investigate the question, Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Zoologist Leila Kowalski set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.30038648dc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-65","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Castellano is an astronomer.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Castellano measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Castellano found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Castellano concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Castellano measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Castellano concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","Astronomer Leila Castellano set out to learn whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.","Castellano found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.6fa7f9b4b0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-77","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Duarte is an economist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Duarte tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Duarte found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Duarte found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","To investigate the question, Duarte tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Economist Nadia Duarte set out to learn whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.967cad23a7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-79","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Vance is a botanist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Vance grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Vance found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Botanist Lucía Vance set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.","Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Vance found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","To investigate the question, Vance grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.af394ee8ea","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-88","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Moreau is an urban planner.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Moreau measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Moreau found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Moreau concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Moreau found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Moreau measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Moreau concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Urban planner Elias Moreau set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.4ee00e109b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-104","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Duarte is a chemist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Duarte placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Duarte found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Duarte placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Chemist Jonas Duarte set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","Duarte found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.9704c14a28","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-126","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Delacroix is a public health researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Delacroix counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Delacroix found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Public health researcher Yara Delacroix set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","To investigate the question, Delacroix counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Delacroix found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","Delacroix concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.644257a9d9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-140","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Novak is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","To investigate the question, Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Neuroscientist Hana Novak set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.","Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.a630424378","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"group":"syn-s-160","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Asante is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Behavioral economist Jonas Asante set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.","Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
